issues.description:
There is a gap in the counting convention, which I can close. F_{≤D} and κ̄_D count functions that are distinct (up to sign) on the sample. But Definition 2.1 does not merge candidates that coincide on the sample. Theorem A1's T must count gates that are distinct as functions on X, because h_t on X depends on every gate with nonzero weight. Under the definitions as written, 'Theorem A1 holds with T = T(t) and T(t) ≤ T̄(t)' is false.

Counterexample (referee_A_r2.out §2): d = 6, n = 4, target par2, first event of the depth-one (LS) race without merging. 24 X-distinct gates fire, but |F_{≤1}| = 6 and T̄ = 2. The min-norm LS predictor over all fired gates differs from the one-representative predictor on 33% of the cube.

The proof is correct once the race merges candidates that coincide (up to sign) on the sample and the readout keeps one representative per class. That is the convention Section 5 already uses ('Candidates that coincide on the sample are merged'). No published number changes. Theorem A2.3 and Corollary A2.5(a) are unaffected, because A2.3 holds for any set B of fired gates, including sample-duplicates.

Everything else in (a′) checks out:
- the principal-submatrix step and the sign-conjugation step;
- monotonicity of L_T;
- the depth-one ‖R‖_n refinement;
- the population value κ̄₁ = d (A^T A is exactly diag(d,…,d,2,…,2) for d = 6, 8, 10, and the full cube gives 7.000000 at d = 7);
- the empirical κ̄₁ (35.3/34.5/35.3 at n = 4096 and 32.6/32.4/32.2 at n = 16384 for three other seeds);
- the table values 0.21/0.41/0.61 and 0.053/0.115/0.195.

(a) A4.2(2) says 'In general, the race stops only when y lies in the span of the fired gates.' That is false as stated. The race also stalls, with y outside the span, when every available candidate has zero utility: par3 in the population (Proposition A4.3(1)) is an example.

(b) A4.3(3) adds 'after which gates fitted to noise fire'. That is not proved: Proposition A2.6 is only a lower bound on the first firing time.

Neither affects the rest of the proofs. I checked A4.2(2)'s new proof line by line and it is complete:
- depth-one utilities vanish against −χ/2;
- the Fourier lemma's case analysis is exhaustive, since any two of the three pairs share exactly one index;
- U = −c₃·\widehat{ab}(123)/2;
- the 12 maximizers and the 6Θ firing time are right;
- each maximizer completes maj3.

The exact recount on the d = 4 cube gives 12 at |U| = 1/4, 20 at 1/8 and 54 nonconstant functions at 0; the note's 55 includes the constant function. An exhaustive search on d = 4 also confirms s* = 3: no 1- or 2-gate consistent circuit exists. That search is complete for all d, because a 2-gate fan-in-2 circuit has at most one input slot left for an irrelevant variable.
